                <note rend="inline" type="source">811.612 Oranges/Spain/—: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Spain</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Moore</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic"
                        >to the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Madrid</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1925-12-09T23:00:00+00:00"><hi rendition="#italic">December 9,
                                1925—11 p.m.</hi></date><lb/>[Received December 9—8:15
                        p.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>76. Has the Department of Agriculture placed an embargo on Spanish oranges? An
                    immediate answer is vital to every American business interest in Spain.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Moore</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
